1. **A collar-mounted acoustic sensing device comprising:**

a housing configured to be supported by a collar;

a metal electrode probe extending through an opening in the housing and having a contact portion positioned to contact a body surface of a wearer;

a piezoelectric element acoustically coupled to the metal electrode probe and configured to generate an electrical signal in response to acoustic vibrations conducted through the metal electrode probe;

a plurality of elastomeric isolation rings disposed around the metal electrode probe and positioned between the metal electrode probe and the housing to mechanically isolate the metal electrode probe from housing-borne vibrations;

a securing grommet received in the opening and configured to retain the metal electrode probe relative to the housing while permitting transmission of the acoustic vibrations from the contact portion to the piezoelectric element; and

a processor disposed within the housing, electrically coupled to the piezoelectric element, and configured to process the electrical signal to detect an acoustic event associated with the wearer.
